---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Miller Lite — Canadian Launch · Noah Barlow"
  description="Directed the Canadian launch of Miller Lite for SABMiller — positioning, packaging, and category strategy in a market that didn't yet exist."
>
  <article class="case shell">
    <header class="case-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Case study · 2014 – 2018</span>
      <h1>Building a light-beer category that didn't exist yet.</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="case-meta">
      <div class="item"><span class="label">Client</span>SABMiller Canada</div>
      <div class="item"><span class="label">Sector</span>Beer · Mass premium</div>
      <div class="item"><span class="label">Role</span>Lead strategist · Brand &amp; launch</div>
      <div class="item"><span class="label">Output</span>Positioning · Pack system · GTM</div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-img">
      <img src="/img/work/miller-lite.jpg" alt="Miller Lite — Canadian launch creative" />
    </div>

    <div class="case-blocks">
      <div class="case-block">
        <div class="label">Problem</div>
        <h3>Canada didn't have a credible light beer.</h3>
        <p>
          Domestic light SKUs were positioned as low-calorie compromises, not
          as a category in their own right. Miller Lite was a 50-year-old
          American icon entering a market that had been taught to read "light"
          as a deficiency.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-block">
        <div class="label">Insight</div>
        <h3>Light is a posture, not a calorie count.</h3>
        <p>
          The American Miller Lite story — "The Original Lite" — wasn't about
          fewer calories. It was about confidence: a beer for people who
          didn't need to perform masculinity. Canada had never been offered
          that posture.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-block">
        <div class="label">Strategy</div>
        <h3>Anchor on heritage. Build a category, not a product.</h3>
        <p>
          We positioned Miller Lite as the founder of the category — the
          original — and built the entire launch around credibility, taste
          credentials, and unambiguous design. We refused the &ldquo;low-cal&rdquo;
          conversation entirely.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-block">
        <div class="label">Execution</div>
        <h3>Packaging system, retail playbook, demand sequencing.</h3>
        <p>
          A pack system built for the cooler door: blue-and-gold confidence,
          oversized wordmark, "Original Lite" lockup as a category signal.
          National retail playbook, on-premise sequencing, founder-led
          launch press, and a paid plan engineered for trial-to-repeat.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-block">
        <div class="label">Outcome</div>
        <h3>From zero to a recognized national brand.</h3>
        <p>
          Miller Lite became one of SABMiller Canada's fastest-growing SKUs
          inside eighteen months, opened the light-beer conversation in
          Canada, and seeded a portfolio approach the broader business
          rebuilt around.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: clamp(3rem,5vw,5rem); padding-top: clamp(2rem,3vw,2.5rem); border-top: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule); max-width: var(--shell-narrow); margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="display:block;">Building a category, or competing in one?</p>
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--t-xl); line-height: 1.3; color: var(--ink); max-width: 32ch; margin-top: 0.85em;">
        Score your brand against the seven moves real challengers actually make.
      </p>
      <div style="margin-top: 1.25rem; display: flex; gap: 0.85rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a href="/scorecard" class="btn hot">Take the Challenger Scorecard &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/diagnostics" class="btn ghost">See all diagnostics</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: clamp(2.5rem,4vw,3.5rem); display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="/work" class="btn ghost">&larr; All work</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn">Work together</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
